  /// valid values are: OFF – Neither Verified Permissions nor Cedar perform
  /// any validation on policies. No validation errors are reported by either
  /// service. STRICT – Requires a schema to be present in the policy store.
  /// Cedar performs validation on all submitted new or updated static
  /// policies and policy templates. Any that fail validation are rejected and
  /// Cedar doesn't store them in the policy store. If Mode=STRICT and the
  /// policy store doesn't contain a schema, Verified Permissions rejects all
  /// static policies and policy templates because there is no schema to
  /// validate against. To submit a static policy or policy template without a
  /// schema, you must turn off validation.
  pub mode: ValidationMode? = None
}
